WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.732 --> 00:00:15.681
It was a very dark night, and a mist hung over the river.

2
00:00:16.802 --> 00:00:19.304
On London Bridge two figures emerged from the mist.

3
00:00:20.464 --> 00:00:24.247
The woman walked quickly and looked eagerly about, as if she were searching for someone.

4
00:00:25.288 --> 00:00:29.971
The boy hung back in the shadows, stopping when she stopped and picking up his pace whenever she

5
00:00:30.031 --> 00:00:30.512
moved on.

6
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.421
The woman walked back and forth on the bridge.

7
00:00:34.502 --> 00:00:39.506
As the clocks chimed midnight, a young lady, accompanied by an old gentleman, emerged from a carriage.

8
00:00:40.586 --> 00:00:42.728
The woman immediately rushed up to Rose and Mr.

9
00:00:42.748 --> 00:00:45.510
Brownlow. "I'm afraid to speak to you here!"

10
00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:46.390
said Nancy.

11
00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.412
"Follow me down these steps."

12
00:00:49.532 --> 00:00:51.233
Hearing this, Bolter ran ahead of them.

13
00:00:52.294 --> 00:00:55.396
He bounded down the steps, which led to a landing overlooking the river.

14
00:00:56.437 --> 00:00:58.098
There he flattened himself against a pillar.

15
00:00:58.118 --> 00:01:01.444
"This is far enough," said Mr.

16
00:01:01.484 --> 00:01:05.527
Brownlow, stopping partway down the dark steps but still within earshot of Bolter.

17
00:01:05.547 --> 00:01:09.189
"Most people would have distrusted you too much to come this far.

18
00:01:10.249 --> 00:01:12.590
Why not let us speak to you on the bridge, where it is light?"

19
00:01:12.611 --> 00:01:16.072
"I'm afraid someone might see us," said Nancy.

20
00:01:16.092 --> 00:01:19.554
"I don't know why, but I have such a sense of dread tonight.

21
00:01:20.675 --> 00:01:22.596
I've been seeing signs of death all evening."

22
00:01:22.616 --> 00:01:25.578
"It's just your imagination," Mr.

23
00:01:25.598 --> 00:01:26.638
Brownlow said soothingly.

24
00:01:26.658 --> 00:01:29.460
"We waited for you on the bridge last Sunday night.

25
00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:31.380
Why didn't you come?"

26
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.701
"I was kept away by the man that I told the lady about.

27
00:01:35.841 --> 00:01:39.282
I only managed to see her the first time because I slipped him a sleeping potion."

28
00:01:40.403 --> 00:01:42.063
Rose gave Nancy a sympathetic look.

29
00:01:43.123 --> 00:01:45.184
"Speak to her kindly," Rose said to Mr.

30
00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:48.305
Brownlow. "The poor creature seems to need that."

31
00:01:48.325 --> 00:01:54.747
"This young lady," he said, indicating Rose, "has told me everything that you communicated to her.

32
00:01:55.887 --> 00:02:01.236
We propose to extract the secret—whatever it may be—from this man Monks.

33
00:02:01.256 --> 00:02:04.277
If he won't cooperate with us, then you must hand Fagin over to us."

34
00:02:04.297 --> 00:02:07.539
"Fagin!" cried Nancy, recoiling.

35
00:02:07.559 --> 00:02:13.861
"Never! As evil as he is and as poorly as he has treated me, I won't turn on

36
00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:16.522
him." "Tell me why," said Mr.

37
00:02:16.562 --> 00:02:18.863
Brownlow, who did not seem surprised by this answer.

38
00:02:18.883 --> 00:02:22.905
"There's a band of us who have lived a bad life together for a long time.

39
00:02:24.065 --> 00:02:26.947
No one has ever turned on me, so I won't do that to any of them."

40
00:02:26.967 --> 00:02:30.852
"Then put Monks into my hands and let me deal with him," Mr.

41
00:02:30.872 --> 00:02:31.673
Brownlow urged her.

42
00:02:31.693 --> 00:02:34.235
"What if he turns against the others?"

43
00:02:34.715 --> 00:02:35.376
Nancy asked.

44
00:02:35.396 --> 00:02:40.300
"I promise you that if the truth is forced from him, the matter will end there.

45
00:02:41.421 --> 00:02:43.022
Your associates will not be harmed."

46
00:02:44.123 --> 00:02:46.025
Nancy did not respond for a few moments.

47
00:02:47.186 --> 00:02:48.507
Finally she turned back to Mr.

48
00:02:48.547 --> 00:02:52.110
Brownlow. "Monks will never find out that I'm the one who told you?"

49
00:02:52.130 --> 00:02:54.351
"Never," vowed Mr.

50
00:02:54.371 --> 00:02:59.836
Brownlow. "The information will be presented to him carefully, and he will never guess where it came from."

51
00:03:00.956 --> 00:03:03.278
After receiving more reassurances from both Mr.

52
00:03:03.298 --> 00:03:06.000
Brownlow and Rose, Nancy began to tell her story.

53
00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.423
She spoke so quietly that it was often difficult for Bolter to overhear what she was saying.

54
00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:15.906
After repeating the story that she had told Rose, Nancy told Mr.

55
00:03:15.926 --> 00:03:17.147
Brownlow where to find Monks.

56
00:03:18.368 --> 00:03:20.750
She described the pub where she had been earlier that night.

57
00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:26.293
Monks frequently went to this pub, Nancy explained, telling them when he was mostly likely to be found

58
00:03:26.313 --> 00:03:30.036
there. "He's a tall man," Nancy went on.

59
00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.781
"As he walks, he constantly looks over his shoulder.

60
00:03:34.901 --> 00:03:39.262
He looks withered and haggard even though he can't be more than 26 or 28 years old.

61
00:03:40.383 --> 00:03:44.844
His lips are often discolored and disfigured with the marks of his teeth because he has desperate fits,

62
00:03:45.044 --> 00:03:46.984
and sometimes he even bites his hands."

63
00:03:47.004 --> 00:03:50.545
"You must be well acquainted with Monks," said Mr.

64
00:03:50.565 --> 00:03:52.446
Brownlow. "No.

65
00:03:53.486 --> 00:03:57.147
I've only seen him twice, and both times he was covered up in a large, dark cloak.

66
00:03:58.327 --> 00:04:00.488
I've drawn out this description from others who know him.

67
00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.381
There's one more thing," she added.

68
00:04:03.401 --> 00:04:10.903
"Upon his throat and sometimes visible below his neckerchief, there is—" "A broad red mark like a burn

69
00:04:10.923 --> 00:04:11.503
or scald?"

70
00:04:11.823 --> 00:04:12.243
cried Mr.

71
00:04:12.283 --> 00:04:14.844
Brownlow. "Yes!"

72
00:04:15.264 --> 00:04:15.844
said Nancy.

73
00:04:15.864 --> 00:04:17.584
"Do you know him?"

74
00:04:17.604 --> 00:04:20.945
"I think I do by your description," said Mr.

75
00:04:20.965 --> 00:04:24.726
Brownlow. "Young woman, you've given us most valuable assistance.

76
00:04:25.867 --> 00:04:27.127
Now what can I do to serve you?"

77
00:04:27.147 --> 00:04:30.428
"Nothing, sir," replied Nancy, weeping.

78
00:04:31.548 --> 00:04:33.189
"I am past all hope indeed."

79
00:04:33.209 --> 00:04:37.731
"We could find you a safe hiding place in England or in another country if you fear to

80
00:04:37.772 --> 00:04:38.392
remain here.

81
00:04:39.492 --> 00:04:41.594
Before dawn you could disappear, leaving no trace.

82
00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:46.416
Come! I won't have you go back to your criminal associates."

83
00:04:47.617 --> 00:04:49.938
"She will be persuaded now," Rose assured him.

84
00:04:50.979 --> 00:04:53.760
But Nancy could not be persuaded to leave London and Bill Sikes.

85
00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:57.162
"I'm chained to my old life," she explained.

86
00:04:57.182 --> 00:05:00.424
"I hate it, but I cannot leave.

87
00:05:01.588 --> 00:05:03.169
I have gone too far to turn back."

88
00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:05.291
She looked around quickly.

89
00:05:05.311 --> 00:05:07.593
"The fear comes over me again.

90
00:05:08.774 --> 00:05:09.615
I must go home."

91
00:05:09.635 --> 00:05:13.658
"Home!" repeated Rose with great stress upon the word.

92
00:05:14.759 --> 00:05:18.282
She couldn't imagine how Nancy could think of her wretched living space as a home.

93
00:05:18.302 --> 00:05:21.164
"To such a home as I have made for myself.

94
00:05:22.265 --> 00:05:25.688
I hope that I have done you a service, and now all I ask is that you leave

95
00:05:25.728 --> 00:05:27.449
me and let me go on my way alone."

96
00:05:27.469 --> 00:05:30.071
"It's useless," said Mr.

97
00:05:30.111 --> 00:05:30.952
Brownlow with a sigh.

98
00:05:32.012 --> 00:05:33.833
"We compromise her safety by staying here.

99
00:05:34.953 --> 00:05:37.234
We may have already detained her longer than she expected."

100
00:05:37.254 --> 00:05:40.054
"Yes, you have," said Nancy.

101
00:05:40.074 --> 00:05:43.656
"This purse," said Rose, holding it out to Nancy.

102
00:05:43.676 --> 00:05:48.257
"Take it for my sake so that you may have some resources in an hour of need."

103
00:05:50.097 --> 00:05:51.838
"No, I have not done this for money.

104
00:05:52.878 --> 00:05:54.239
Let me console myself with that.

105
00:05:55.199 --> 00:05:58.300
If you want to give me something, let it be a small reminder of you."

106
00:05:59.484 --> 00:06:01.925
Rose held out a ring to Nancy, but she refused it.

107
00:06:03.025 --> 00:06:05.426
Rose then offered a handkerchief, which Nancy accepted.

108
00:06:05.446 --> 00:06:08.346
"Bless you, good lady," said Nancy.

109
00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:09.887
"Good night."

110
00:06:11.027 --> 00:06:12.868
Mr. Brownlow and Rose climbed the steps.

111
00:06:14.148 --> 00:06:18.469
As they disappeared across the bridge, Nancy sat down on the steps and vented the anguish of her

112
00:06:18.509 --> 00:06:19.710
heart in bitter tears.

113
00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:23.371
After a while she arose and ascended to the street.

114
00:06:24.451 --> 00:06:28.012
Astonished by what he had heard, Bolter remained hidden for a few more minutes.

115
00:06:29.192 --> 00:06:32.776
Then, glancing cautiously around, he stealthily returned to the bridge.

116
00:06:33.998 --> 00:06:38.803
Once he reached the street, Bolter ran for Fagin's house as fast as his legs could carry him.
